        observations: ['Monitor power draw and variability','Track bearing pad temperatures','Listen for abnormal grinding sounds','Check pebble crusher performance','Measure product size consistently'],
        safety: ['The SAG mill represents an extreme rotating mass hazard, as the shell can be up to 12 meters in diameter and weigh thousands of tons when loaded with ore and balls; any contact with the rotating shell, girth gear, or associated drive components will result in instant fatal injury.','Multiple lockout/tagout points must be secured before any maintenance activity, including the gearless drive or ring motor, inching drive, lubrication systems, and hydraulic brakes, because the enormous stored energy in the rotating mass requires positive isolation at every energy source to prevent unexpected movement.','No person shall enter the SAG mill interior without completing full multi-point energy isolation, installation of mechanical brakes or blocking devices, atmospheric testing, and establishment of a confined space entry permit, as the combination of extreme rotating mass, heavy media, and confined space creates multiple immediately-life-threatening hazards.','Only personnel who have completed specialized SAG mill maintenance training shall perform work on or inside the mill, as the unique hazards of gearless drives, hydrostatic bearings, massive liner segments, and confined space operations require specific knowledge and skills beyond general industrial maintenance qualifications.','Emergency stop systems including clearly marked e-stop buttons at all access points, pull cords around the mill perimeter, and automated protection systems must be maintained in fully functional condition at all times, as the enormous energy stored in the rotating mill requires immediate shutdown capability to prevent catastrophic injuries during upset conditions.']
