        observations: ['Check pebble size distribution','Monitor media consumption rate','Track product quality for contamination','Measure grinding efficiency','Inspect liner condition'],
        safety: ['Pebble mills present the same fundamental hazards as conventional ball mills including the extreme danger of the rotating shell and grinding charge; all personnel must treat this equipment with the same level of caution and follow identical safety protocols as for steel-media tumbling mills.','Complete lockout/tagout (LOTO) procedures must be performed on all energy sources including the main drive, inching drive, and auxiliary systems before any person enters the mill interior, as unexpected rotation of the shell with the heavy pebble charge will cause fatal crushing injuries.','Entry into the pebble mill for inspection, cleaning, or liner replacement constitutes a confined space entry requiring a formal entry permit, atmospheric monitoring for oxygen and toxic gases, continuous ventilation, a trained standby attendant, and rescue equipment immediately available at the entry point.','Pebble media handling operations must use proper mechanical equipment and ergonomic practices, as the repeated manual handling of heavy rock pebbles weighing several kilograms each can cause serious musculoskeletal injuries, and bulk pebble storage and transport create risks of burial and crushing.','All personnel working near the pebble mill must wear both hearing protection rated for high-decibel environments and respiratory protection appropriate for the dust generated, as the tumbling pebble media generates hazardous noise levels exceeding 95 dB and the grinding action produces fine airborne dust that can cause chronic respiratory disease.']
