        observations: ['Monitor vibration amplitude','Check spring condition','Track power consumption','Inspect media levels','Measure product fineness'],
        safety: ['No person should touch or make physical contact with the vibratory mill during operation, as the high-frequency vibration at 900-1500 RPM with amplitudes of 2-10mm can cause hand-arm vibration syndrome, fatigue fractures, internal organ damage, and severe physiological harm even from brief contact.','Noise levels generated by vibratory mills during operation are extremely high, often exceeding 100 dB, and all personnel in the area must be made aware of the noise hazard through posted warnings and designated hearing protection zones to prevent permanent noise-induced hearing loss.','Complete lockout/tagout (LOTO) procedures must be performed on the vibration drive motor and all energy sources before opening the grinding chamber or performing any maintenance, as the high-frequency vibrating components can cause severe injuries from impact, trapping, or entanglement if the mill is energized.','The vibratory mill must be installed on a properly engineered foundation with adequate isolation springs and vibration damping, as an inadequate foundation can allow destructive resonance, excessive vibration transmission to surrounding structures, and potential catastrophic failure of the mill supports.','All personnel working in the vicinity of the vibratory mill must wear hearing protection such as dual-protection earmuffs over earplugs rated for at least 105 dB, as the intense high-frequency vibration generates extremely high noise levels that can cause immediate hearing damage and permanent hearing loss even with brief unprotected exposure.']
