        safety: ['The safety enclosure must be fully closed, latched, and verified secure before starting the planetary mill, as the high centrifugal forces up to 100g can cause catastrophic jar ejection if a clamp fails, and an unsecured jar would become a lethal high-velocity projectile.','Grinding jar and ball materials must be carefully selected for chemical compatibility with the sample being processed, as incompatible materials can cause violent exothermic reactions, corrosion-induced jar failure, or contamination of the sample with hazardous reaction products.','When grinding reactive, volatile, or gas-generating materials, jars equipped with pressure relief valves must be used, as sealed jars can develop dangerous internal pressures from chemical reactions, thermal expansion, or gas evolution, potentially causing explosive rupture and release of hazardous contents.','Grinding jars must be handled with insulated gloves or tongs after milling cycles, as the intense energy input from planetary motion generates significant heat that can raise jar temperatures high enough to cause serious burns upon direct skin contact.','Eye protection such as safety goggles or a face shield must be worn when opening grinding jars after a milling cycle, as pressurized gases may escape suddenly, fine dust can become airborne, and reactive samples may have created volatile or irritating compounds that can cause serious eye injuries.']
