        safety: ['The scraped surface heat exchanger contains a rotating shaft with scraper blades inside the processing cylinder, and complete lockout/tagout must be performed before opening the unit for any reason, as the rotating shaft and blades can cause severe laceration, entanglement, and crushing injuries if the drive starts unexpectedly.','The outer surface of the heated or cooled cylinder and associated jacket piping may be at extreme temperatures ranging from sub-zero for crystallization to over 200 degrees C for heating, and appropriate insulation, warning signs, and temperature-appropriate PPE must be used to prevent burn or cold-contact injuries.','Shaft seal failure will release process product to the exterior of the unit, and when handling hazardous, hot, or pressurized products, appropriate containment, drip trays, and leak detection must be installed, as seal leakage can cause chemical burns, slip hazards, and exposure to toxic materials.','The drive system delivers high torque to the scraper shaft to overcome the resistance of viscous products against the cylinder wall, and all drive components including couplings, gearboxes, and shafts must be properly guarded, as the high-torque rotating elements can cause severe entanglement and crushing injuries upon contact.','Internal cleaning of the scraped surface heat exchanger cylinder constitutes a confined space entry requiring a formal permit, atmospheric testing, continuous ventilation, and a standby attendant, as the enclosed cylindrical space may contain residual hazardous product, cleaning chemicals, or an oxygen-depleted atmosphere.']
