        observations: ['Check vertical tube temp profile','Monitor burner flames','Track convection section DP','Verify refractory integrity','Watch for tube sagging'],
        safety: ['The vertical cylindrical design of this heater creates significant fall hazards when personnel access elevated platforms for tube inspection, convection section maintenance, or stack work, and proper fall protection including guardrails, safety harnesses, and tie-off points must be used at all times when working above grade.','The external surfaces of the cylindrical shell, convection section, and stack at elevated levels are at very high temperatures, and work at these heights combines burn hazards with fall hazards; appropriate heat-resistant PPE and fall protection must be used simultaneously, and hot work at height requires additional safety planning.','The floor-fired upward burner configuration creates a flame hazard at ground level where personnel access the heater for burner maintenance, and proper procedures must be followed to ensure all burners are safely shut down and the firebox is purged before any person approaches the burner openings, as direct exposure to burner flames causes instant fatal burns.','Entry into the firebox of the cylindrical heater for inspection, tube examination, or refractory repair constitutes confined space entry requiring a formal permit, atmospheric monitoring for O2, CO, H2S, and combustible gases, forced ventilation, continuous communication, a standby attendant, and rescue equipment at the entry point.','Burner light-off procedures must be strictly followed according to NFPA 86 or equivalent standards, including proper firebox purging with a minimum of four volume changes, pilot flame verification, and sequential burner ignition, as failure to properly purge the firebox before ignition can result in a catastrophic firebox explosion.']
