        troubles: [{p:'Fouling',c:'Low velocity, hot surfaces, scaling salts',a:'Increase circulation, reduce temp, treat water'},{p:'Pump problems',c:'Cavitation, wear, seal failure',a:'Check NPSH, replace wear parts, fix seal'},{p:'Entrainment',c:'High vapor velocity, small separator',a:'Reduce rate, add demister, check separator'},{p:'Low capacity',c:'Fouled exchanger, pump wear, low steam',a:'Clean HX, check pump, verify steam'}],
        observations: ['Monitor circulation rate','Check pump condition','Track heat transfer coefficient','Verify separator level','Watch for entrainment'],
        safety: ['Multiple hot surfaces on the forced circulation evaporator including the heat exchanger shell, steam piping, flash vessel, and connecting piping operate at elevated temperatures, and appropriate insulation, warning signs, and heat-resistant PPE must be provided to prevent burn injuries to operating and maintenance personnel.','The circulation pump must be properly isolated with lockout/tagout procedures before any maintenance work, including closing and locking suction and discharge valves and depressurizing the pump casing, as the pump operates at high flow rates with hot process fluid under pressure, and unexpected startup or fluid release can cause severe burns and injuries.','The flash vessel and heat exchanger are pressure vessels operating at elevated temperature and pressure, and all safety devices including relief valves, level controls, and pressure indicators must be maintained in proper working condition, as a pressure vessel failure can cause catastrophic release of hot fluid and steam with fatal blast and burn consequences.','Personnel working on the forced circulation evaporator may be exposed to the process chemicals being concentrated, which may be corrosive, toxic, or otherwise hazardous, and appropriate chemical-resistant PPE including face protection, gloves, and protective clothing must be worn, especially when taking samples, opening connections, or cleaning the system.','Live steam at high temperature and pressure is used as the heating medium, and all steam connections, control valves, traps, and condensate lines must be properly maintained, as steam leaks can cause severe burns that may not be immediately visible because steam is transparent, and contact with even low-pressure steam causes instant scalding injuries.']
