        observations: ['Check tube wetting','Monitor outlet temperature','Track steam consumption','Verify feed distribution','Watch for foaming'],
        safety: ['The long vertical tubes of the rising film evaporator are heated by steam and contain boiling process fluid, making all tube surfaces and associated steam chests extremely hot; appropriate insulation, warning signs, and heat-resistant PPE must be used, as contact with these surfaces will cause severe burn injuries.','The rising film evaporator body, steam chest, and vapor head are pressure vessels that must be properly rated, inspected, and equipped with functional relief devices, as failure of any pressure-containing component can result in catastrophic release of hot process fluid and steam with fatal burn and blast consequences.','Chemical cleaning of the evaporator tubes is regularly required to remove scale and fouling deposits, and all chemical cleaning operations must follow strict procedures including chemical compatibility verification, appropriate corrosion-resistant PPE, proper ventilation, neutralization, and waste disposal, as the cleaning chemicals are typically strong acids that cause severe burns.','The vapor outlet from the rising film evaporator carries hot process vapor that may contain entrained product droplets, and all vapor piping connections, gaskets, and relief devices must be properly maintained, as a vapor release can cause steam burns and exposure to concentrated product chemicals, particularly during startup or upset conditions.','The rising film evaporator with tubes 4-10 meters long is a tall unit requiring work at height for feed distribution, instrumentation, and vapor head access; proper fall protection including guardrails, safety harnesses, and secured work platforms must be provided for all elevated work.']
