        safety: ['The heated vertical tubes, steam jacket, and associated piping of the falling film evaporator operate at elevated temperatures, and all hot surfaces must be insulated and marked with warning signs, with heat-resistant PPE required for personnel, as contact with heated components will cause burn injuries.','The falling film evaporator is often used for food-grade or pharmaceutical products where contamination must be prevented, and strict hygienic procedures, proper gasket selection, and sanitary design standards must be followed to prevent product contamination that could pose health risks to end consumers.','Chemical cleaning of the evaporator tubes and distribution system must follow validated procedures with compatible cleaning agents, appropriate PPE, proper ventilation, and thorough rinsing verification, as residual cleaning chemicals can contaminate the next production batch, and the cleaning chemicals themselves pose burn and inhalation hazards to maintenance personnel.','Falling film evaporators often operate under vacuum to reduce boiling temperatures for heat-sensitive products, and all vacuum-rated components must be designed for full vacuum conditions, as vacuum collapse can cause implosion of the vessel, and opening connections on a vacuum system can cause sudden inrush of air and fluid that creates impact and splash hazards.','The liquid distribution system at the top of the falling film evaporator requires periodic access for inspection, cleaning, and adjustment at significant height, and proper fall protection including safety harnesses, guardrails, and secured work platforms must be provided, as falls from the distribution level are potentially fatal.']
