        observations: ['Watch circulation patterns','Check steam trap operation','Monitor product concentration','Track heat transfer','Verify level control'],
        safety: ['The calandria evaporator has extensive hot surfaces throughout including the steam chest, short tubes, vapor space walls, and all associated piping, and comprehensive insulation and warning signs must be provided, as the large surface area at boiling temperatures creates widespread burn hazards for personnel working in the vicinity.','The calandria evaporator contains a large inventory of hot process liquid at or near boiling temperature, and any failure of the vessel, piping, or fittings can result in a massive release of scalding fluid; proper pressure relief, level controls, and containment must be maintained to protect personnel from catastrophic hot liquid release.','The steam chest operates at elevated pressure to provide the driving force for evaporation, and all steam connections, controls, relief devices, and condensate systems must be properly maintained and regularly inspected, as a steam-side failure can cause violent release of high-temperature steam with fatal burn consequences.','Entry into the calandria evaporator body for tube cleaning, inspection, or descaling constitutes confined space entry requiring a formal permit, atmospheric testing, forced ventilation, a standby attendant, and rescue equipment, as the enclosed vessel may contain residual process chemicals, oxygen-depleted atmospheres, or cleaning chemical fumes.','The area around the calandria evaporator and especially the access platforms, ladders, and vessel interior can become extremely slippery from condensation, spilled product, and cleaning solutions, and proper non-slip flooring, drainage, and footwear must be provided to prevent slip and fall injuries that are particularly dangerous near hot equipment.']
