        observations: ['Monitor compressor operation','Track power consumption','Check temperature approaches','Verify non-condensable venting','Watch for compressor surge'],
        safety: ['The mechanical vapor recompression compressor is a high-speed rotating machine that requires proper guarding on all rotating components, vibration monitoring, and lockout/tagout before any maintenance, as contact with the rotating impeller, shaft, or coupling can cause fatal entanglement and laceration injuries.','The MVR system relies on significant electrical power for the vapor compressor, and all electrical systems including the motor, variable frequency drive, controls, and power cables must be properly rated, maintained, and protected, as electrical faults in the high-power drive system can cause electrocution, arc flash burns, and fire.','The compressor discharge piping, condensing surfaces, and associated piping operate at elevated temperatures due to the recompressed vapor, and appropriate insulation and warning signs must be provided, as contact with hot surfaces in the tight confines typical of MVR installations can cause serious burn injuries.','The MVR system contains pressure vessels and piping operating at the elevated pressure created by the vapor compressor, and all pressure-containing components must be properly rated and equipped with relief devices, as overpressure from compressor malfunction or downstream blockage can cause catastrophic vessel failure.','The vapor compressor is susceptible to surge, bearing failure, and seal leakage, all of which can cause rapid release of hot vapor, mechanical destruction of the compressor internals, and ejection of fragments; proper anti-surge protection, vibration monitoring, and temperature alarms must be maintained to prevent catastrophic compressor failures.']
