        observations: ['Monitor temperature profile','Check agitator operation','Track reaction progress','Verify additions complete','Watch pressure behavior'],
        safety: ['Exothermic runaway reactions in batch reactors can rapidly escalate temperature and pressure beyond safe limits, potentially leading to vessel rupture, explosion, or toxic release, so reaction monitoring, emergency cooling systems, and automatic shutdown interlocks must be fully operational at all times.','Pressure relief devices including safety valves and rupture discs must be properly sized, regularly tested, and never blocked or isolated during operation, as they are the last line of defense against catastrophic vessel overpressure during reaction upsets or cooling failures.','Personnel must wear appropriate chemical-resistant PPE including gloves, splash-proof goggles, and face shields when charging reactants, sampling, or discharging products, as direct contact with reactive chemicals can cause severe chemical burns, toxic absorption through skin, or allergic sensitization.','The rotating agitator shaft and impeller present a serious entanglement hazard, and all access points to the vessel interior must be interlocked with the agitator drive so that the agitator cannot start while the vessel is open, with complete lockout/tagout required before any internal work.','Reactor vessel surfaces, jackets, and associated piping may be extremely hot during exothermic reactions or extremely cold during cryogenic processes, and all personnel must wear appropriate thermal protective equipment and be aware of which surfaces are at hazardous temperatures to prevent burn or frostbite injuries.']
