        observations: ['Check dust accumulation','Monitor outlet loading','Verify gas distribution','Watch for buildup','Track hopper discharge'],
        safety: ['Gravity settling chambers are large enclosed spaces that constitute confined spaces with potential for oxygen deficiency, accumulation of toxic or flammable gases, and residual hazardous dust, requiring full confined space entry procedures including atmospheric testing, ventilation, and rescue standby for any internal access.','Hot process gas flowing through the settling chamber heats all internal surfaces and structural components to temperatures that can cause severe burns on contact, and personnel must verify that the chamber has cooled to safe temperatures before entry, with thermal protective equipment required for any work near hot gas connections.','Accumulated dust disturbed during cleaning, maintenance, or hopper discharge becomes airborne and can be inhaled, causing respiratory damage, and some dusts are toxic, carcinogenic, or fibrogenic, requiring respiratory protection, dust suppression measures, and proper PPE when working in or near the settling chamber.','The interior of large gravity settling chambers may require working at heights on internal baffles, support structures, or ladders, where fall protection systems, secure footing, and compliance with working-at-height regulations are essential to prevent potentially fatal falls onto hard surfaces.','Manual or mechanical removal of accumulated dust from hoppers and chamber floors exposes workers to dust inhalation, heavy material handling injuries, and potential engulfment if large quantities of accumulated material shift unexpectedly, requiring proper dust extraction equipment, stable footing, and awareness of overhead material hazards.']
