        safety: ['The rotating helical screw inside the trough presents a severe entanglement and amputation hazard, so all guards and covers must remain securely in place during operation and no personnel should reach into the trough while the screw is turning.','Never open or remove trough covers while the screw conveyor is running, as the exposed rotating flight can catch clothing, tools, or limbs and pull them into the mechanism, causing catastrophic injury.','Always perform complete lockout/tagout (LOTO) procedures on all energy sources including electrical, mechanical, and pneumatic before beginning any maintenance, inspection, or cleaning work on the screw conveyor, as residual energy or unexpected startup can be fatal.','Personnel working near screw conveyors handling dry powders or granules must wear appropriate respiratory protection such as dust masks or respirators, as airborne particulate generated during conveying can cause respiratory irritation, silicosis, or other chronic lung conditions depending on the material.','When the screw conveyor is used for heated material processing, external trough surfaces can reach temperatures sufficient to cause severe burns on contact, so hot surface warning signs must be posted and personnel must wear heat-resistant gloves when working near the equipment.']
