        safety: ['Working on or near bucket elevators involves significant fall risks due to the height of the structure, so proper fall protection equipment including harnesses, lanyards, and anchor points must be used whenever personnel access elevated platforms, ladders, or the head section.','The continuously moving buckets and belt or chain create severe pinch, entanglement, and crushing hazards, so all access doors and guards must remain closed and secured during operation and no one should ever reach into the casing while the elevator is running.','The interior of the bucket elevator casing is a confined space that may contain hazardous atmospheres including residual dust or oxygen-deficient air, so confined space entry procedures with atmospheric testing, ventilation, and a standby attendant must be followed before anyone enters.','Bucket elevators handling combustible dusts such as grain, sugar, or chemical powders are at high risk of dust explosions, so explosion venting, proper grounding, bearing temperature monitoring, and alignment checks must be maintained to prevent ignition sources.','Material can fall from height within the elevator casing or from the discharge point, so hard hats must be worn in the area and personnel must never stand beneath open inspection doors or the boot section during operation.']
