        observations: ['Monitor pressure drop','Check air velocity','Verify receiver level','Watch for plugging signs','Track filter condition'],
        safety: ['Pneumatic conveying systems handling combustible powders or dusts present a serious dust explosion hazard, so all components must be properly grounded, explosion relief vents must be maintained, and the system should only be operated with appropriate dust concentration monitoring and inerting where required.','The conveying lines and pressure vessels in pneumatic systems operate under significant pressure, so personnel must never open or disconnect any pressurized component without first isolating and depressurizing the system, as sudden release of pressure can cause severe injury from flying debris or material blowout.','Air movers such as blowers and compressors used in pneumatic conveying generate noise levels that frequently exceed 90 dB, so all personnel working in the vicinity must wear appropriate hearing protection such as earplugs or earmuffs to prevent permanent hearing damage from prolonged exposure.','Static electricity can accumulate rapidly in pneumatic conveying systems due to particle-to-particle and particle-to-pipe friction, creating ignition risk in the presence of combustible dust, so all piping, fittings, and equipment must be properly bonded and grounded with verified continuity.','Conveying lines can rupture due to erosion at bends, pressure surges, or material blockages, potentially releasing high-velocity material and pressurized air into the surrounding area, so line thickness must be regularly inspected and personnel should avoid standing near bends and high-wear areas during operation.']
