        observations: ['Monitor motor amps','Check air leakage','Verify feed rate','Listen for grinding','Watch hopper level'],
        safety: ['The rotating rotor with vanes inside the rotary feeder housing creates severe shearing and crushing hazards that can amputate fingers or hands, so all guards must be in place and the inlet and outlet must never be accessed while the rotor is turning.','Never reach into the inlet or outlet of a rotary feeder during operation or while the rotor can still move, as the tight clearance between the rotating vanes and housing will crush or sever any body part that enters the mechanism.','Always perform complete lockout/tagout (LOTO) procedures on all energy sources including the motor, drive, and any connected pneumatic conveying system before performing any maintenance, cleaning, or inspection on the rotary feeder, as unexpected startup or back-pressure driven rotation can cause fatal injuries.','Rotary feeders handling dry bulk powders generate airborne dust at the inlet and outlet connections, so personnel must wear appropriate respiratory protection and dust collection systems must be operational to prevent inhalation exposure to potentially hazardous particulate matter.','When replacing shear pins on the rotary feeder, ensure the unit is fully locked out and the rotor is blocked from rotating, as stored energy from material weight above the feeder or residual pneumatic pressure can cause sudden unexpected rotor movement during the replacement procedure.']
