        observations: ['Monitor feed rate','Check vibration level','Verify material flow','Listen for changes','Watch controller settings'],
        safety: ['Prolonged exposure to vibration from vibratory feeders can cause hand-arm vibration syndrome and other musculoskeletal disorders, so personnel must minimize direct contact with vibrating components and use anti-vibration gloves when physical contact with the equipment is necessary during adjustment or maintenance.','Vibratory feeders have multiple pinch points at the spring mounts, tray supports, and drive connections where fingers or hands can be crushed, so all guards must remain securely in place during operation and lockout/tagout procedures must be completed before any hands-on maintenance work.','All personnel working in the vicinity of vibratory feeders must wear appropriate hearing protection such as earplugs or earmuffs, as the operational noise from vibrating trays and electromagnetic drives typically exceeds 85 dB and prolonged exposure can cause permanent hearing damage.','Electromagnetic vibratory feeders generate strong electromagnetic fields near the drive coils that can interfere with cardiac pacemakers and other implanted medical devices, so personnel with such devices must be warned and kept at a safe distance from the equipment during operation.','The electromagnetic drive coils on vibratory feeders can reach elevated surface temperatures during continuous operation, posing a burn hazard to anyone performing maintenance or adjustments near the drive unit, so personnel should allow adequate cooling time or wear thermal protection gloves before handling coil components.']
