        components: ['Compressor - pressure generation','Aftercooler - heat removal','Dryer - moisture removal','Receiver - storage buffer','Filters - particulate removal','Drain Traps - moisture removal','Distribution - piping network','Regulators - point of use'],
        troubles: [{p:'Low pressure',c:'Leaks, demand, compressor',a:'Fix leaks, check capacity'},{p:'Wet air',c:'Dryer failure, overload',a:'Repair dryer, reduce load'},{p:'Oil carryover',c:'Separator failure',a:'Replace separator, check oil'},{p:'Compressor trip',c:'High temperature, pressure',a:'Check cooling, controls'}],
        observations: ['Monitor system pressure','Check dewpoint','Verify compressor operation','Watch for leaks','Track energy use'],
        safety: ['Compressed air systems operate at pressures that can cause severe injury or death if a pressure vessel, fitting, or hose fails, and high-pressure air directed at the body can cause air embolism through skin breaks, so all components must be rated for the system pressure, safety relief devices must be maintained, and compressed air must never be directed at personnel.','Compressors contain rotating components including shafts, couplings, flywheels, and belt drives that create entanglement, pinch, and shearing hazards, so all rotating parts must be fitted with fixed guards, complete lockout/tagout must be performed before any maintenance, and personnel must never reach near rotating components while the compressor is running.','Air compressors and their associated blowers, motors, and aftercoolers generate noise levels that frequently exceed 90 dB, so all personnel working in compressor rooms or near outdoor compressor installations must wear appropriate hearing protection such as earplugs or earmuffs to prevent permanent hearing damage from prolonged exposure.','Compressor discharge piping, aftercoolers, and inter-stage piping operate at temperatures that can cause severe burns on contact, particularly on reciprocating and screw compressors where discharge temperatures can exceed 150 degrees Celsius, so hot surface guards and warning labels must be maintained and thermal protective gloves must be worn during maintenance.','High-pressure oil injection injury can occur when lubricating oil under compressor discharge pressure is released through a pinhole leak, forcing oil through the skin and into tissue, causing severe injury requiring immediate surgical treatment, so all pressurized oil lines must be inspected for leaks and personnel must never run hands along pressurized oil lines to check for leaks.']
