        observations: ['Monitor pressure','Check for liquids','Verify heating value','Watch for leaks','Track consumption'],
        safety: ['Fuel gas systems contain flammable gas under pressure that can form explosive mixtures with air, and any release of fuel gas can lead to fire or explosion with lethal consequences, so all components must be maintained leak-free, the system must be regularly surveyed with gas detectors, and smoking and open flames must be prohibited in fuel gas areas.','Fuel gas piping and equipment present a serious explosion risk if gas leaks into enclosed spaces and reaches the lower explosive limit concentration, so fixed gas detection must be installed in enclosed fuel gas areas, ventilation must be adequate to prevent gas accumulation, and emergency ventilation procedures must be established.','Regular fuel gas leak detection surveys must be performed using portable combustible gas detectors on all flanges, valves, connections, and instrument fittings, as even small leaks can accumulate to dangerous concentrations in enclosed areas, and any detected leak must be reported and repaired promptly following safe work procedures.','Emergency shutoff valves must be installed in fuel gas supply systems and must be accessible, clearly marked, and tested regularly, so that fuel gas supply can be rapidly isolated in case of fire, explosion, or uncontrolled gas release, and all operators must know the location and operation of emergency shutoff valves in their area.','Work inside fuel gas piping, vessels, or knockout drums constitutes confined space entry in an environment that may contain flammable or oxygen-deficient atmospheres, requiring a confined space entry permit, atmospheric testing and continuous monitoring, positive isolation and blinding, thorough purging with inert gas followed by air, and a standby attendant with rescue equipment.']
